course: dictionary
lesson: 4738
title: Horrible and its friends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Horrible means very bad or unpleasant. It can also mean unkind, or very frightening. The words around it show you which meaning fits. «The milk smelled horrible» tells you the smell was very bad.
explain: The clues in a sentence can change the meaning. «He was horrible to me in the playground» means he was unkind. A lullaby is a soft song for sleeping, so «a horrible lullaby» about beating a boy is shocking, not sweet.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a word such as awful, terrible, dreadful or nasty. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Horrible is an adjective: horrible, more horrible, most horrible.
fact: Horribly is the adverb, as in «horribly wrong».
fact: Horrible can mean very bad, unkind, or very frightening and shocking.
fact: Similar words include awful, terrible, dreadful and nasty.
fact: Horrible is spelled with -ible because horr is not a word on its own.
exercise: «The Duchess sings the baby a horrible lullaby about beating a boy.» What does horrible mean here? | Lovely and calm | Gentle and soft | *Shocking and cruel, not sweet | Very funny
exercise: «He was horrible to me in the playground.» What does horrible mean here? | Lost and sleepy | Very quiet | *Unkind and nasty | Kind and helpful
exercise: Which word could replace horrible in «a horrible smell» and keep the meaning? | Lovely | Gentle | Tiny | *Awful
test: Which word is closest in meaning to horrible? | Happy | Quiet | Tidy | *Dreadful
test: Which word is the adverb of horrible, as in «horribly wrong»? | *Horribly | Horror | Horrid | Horrible
exam: Why is horrible spelled with -ible? | Because it is a verb | Because it always follows a whole word | *Because horr is not a word on its own | Because it means happy
